                <pb facs="0275" n="266" sameAs="frus:frus1938v05/pg266"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">715.1715/1318: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Special Representative of the President</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Corrigan</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">San
                                José</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-08-30T14:00:00-06:00">August 30, 1938—2
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 4 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>84. Zuniga Montufar wishes to postpone any action regarding the
                    Honduran–Nicaraguan controversy because he will be completely occupied during an
                    undetermined part of the month of September with the Panama-Costa Rica boundary
                    settlement (reference special mission despatch No. 99 of August 23rd).<anchor
                        n="55" xml:id="d257-f1"/> His attitude is satisfactory and he has agreed to
                    devote the month of October to the work of the Mediation Commission. He has
                    tentatively agreed to the whole program <pb facs="0276" n="267" xml:id="pg267"/>
                    which I outlined but wishes to have the sanction of President Cortes before
                    making a definite commitment. I am staying over for a conference which he has
                    arranged with the President and will leave San José on Thursday.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Corrigan</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
